      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I want to clarify how I observed this:  was in a crowded instance but had decent (>30) fps.  I had my menu open in my left hand and with my right, my raycast happened to intersect a capsule directly in front of me that was otherwise invisible.  The capsule belonged to someone I had blocked and I could then see their social details in my menu.  Their nameplate details also flashed a few frames above their capsule during this process.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-04-06T01:51:50.201Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If you are in the same room as a user you have blocked, you can still select their capsule with the menu open and see their position.  I am extremely concerned that this is also the case that someone who is blocked may be able to do that to someone who blocked them, which would enable them to follow and harass with pickups or by targeting the people around the blocker.",
